WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.488
Every person needs one key the
agency controls and never changes.

2
00:00:04.488 --> 00:00:05.399
Here's why.

3
00:00:05.399 --> 00:00:09.625
It's tempting to use the HR system's
own person number as the key.

4
00:00:09.625 --> 00:00:13.233
But that number changes
when the HR system changes,

5
00:00:13.233 --> 00:00:15.725
and Core HCM is exactly that change.

6
00:00:15.725 --> 00:00:17.550
Contractors come from elsewhere.

7
00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:21.809
So pick an enterprise key, often
an identifier you already have,

8
00:00:21.809 --> 00:00:23.938
and map every other number to it.

9
00:00:23.938 --> 00:00:28.350
Then the move to the new platform changes
one mapping, and nothing downstream.

10
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:32.178
A returning employee is the same
person, not a new identity,

11
00:00:32.178 --> 00:00:35.288
and a contractor who
converts keeps one record.

12
00:00:35.288 --> 00:00:38.438
And the Social Security
number is never the join key.

13
00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:42.351
The governance body makes this
call before Phase 1 closes.

14
00:00:42.351 --> 00:00:44.020
Next, the standard.
